{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HK47kDF29HzZ1UZ1XWb7wH","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (87.6KB). Full output saved to: /home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/1f691966-10aa-49ba-9a5a-93650aac521b/tool-results/b4br7itst.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\nrtifact\": \"evidence.zip\", \"answer_format\": {\"kind\": \"enum\", \"accepted_values\": [\"true\", \"false\"]}, \"normalization\": \"exact\"}, {\"id\": \"d07_analysis_method_count\", \"question\": \"In evidence.zip, Use all d07-- members in ZIP central-directory order. For Day 7 use the manifest Main-Class classfile; for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit. Submit its classfile method-table count in base 10.\",\n==\n\": \"enum\", \"accepted_values\": [\"true\", \"false\"]}, \"normalization\": \"exact\"}, {\"id\": \"d07_analysis_method_count\", \"question\": \"In evidence.zip, Use all d07-- members in ZIP central-directory order. For Day 7 use the manifest Main-Class classfile; for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit. Submit its classfile method-table count in base 10.\", \"artifact\": \"evidence.zip\", \"answer_format\": {\"ki\n==\n# Coverage atlas -- binary-reverse-engineering (as of D19 post-run, 2026-10-19)\n\nScope: what a D20+ `evidence.zip` group (or backfilled old-group id) could be, how we would recognise it, which standard tool answers it, and how ready we\nare. Grounded in `reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md` (lane log D1-D19), `challenges/day19/binary-jack-in-the-box/solver/`,\n`lib/binary.py` (`hcfg_scan`/`hcfg_find`, `packer_info`, `unpack_upx`, `go_buildinfo`, `go_pclntab_funcs`, `rustfilt`, `macho_facts`,\n`recover_return_constants`, `ghidra_decompile`, `jar_app_classes`, `wasm_layout`) and `tests/data/binary_fixtures/TARGETS.json` (all 9 targets have fixtures).\n\nProgression so far: D1-D14 = one new compiled language per day (container nearly always ELF64 x86