{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XK8KSWeP52iFBFykunFboT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coverage atlas -- binary-reverse-engineering (as of D19 post-run, 2026-10-19)\n2\t\n3\tScope: what a D20+ `evidence.zip` group (or backfilled old-group id) could be, how we would recognise it, which standard tool answers it, and how ready we\n4\tare. Grounded in `reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md` (lane log D1-D19), `challenges/day19/binary-jack-in-the-box/solver/`,\n5\t`lib/binary.py` (`hcfg_scan`/`hcfg_find`, `packer_info`, `unpack_upx`, `go_buildinfo`, `go_pclntab_funcs`, `rustfilt`, `macho_facts`,\n6\t`recover_return_constants`, `ghidra_decompile`, `jar_app_classes`, `wasm_layout`) and `tests/data/binary_fixtures/TARGETS.json` (all 9 targets have fixtures).\n7\t\n8\tProgression so far: D1-D14 = one new compiled language per day (container nearly always ELF64 x86-64, HCFG blob re-stored per\n9\tlanguage); D15-D16 = \"ONE SOURCE, TWO BUILDS\" pairs with a `<qualifier>_` id prefix (`stripped`/`symbolized`, `compact`/`direct`);\n10\tD17 Ada ELF + BACKFILL #2 (160 -> 204 ids: old days' single-solve facts re-asked on their groups + the `hcfg_storage` enum after a\n11\tmid-day contract revision); D18 Fortran ELF (theme \"call graph / no injection\" unasked, CORRECT T+11 s). **D19 \"Jack in the Box\"\n12\t(static-unpacking)** = ONE GnuCOBOL ELF (11 KB, `libcob.so.1`, stripped) whose HCFG is NOT in the image: a `PK19` overlay is\n13\tappended after the section-header table (`PK19|ver|k1|k2|pad|u32le len|sha256[32]|packed`, unpack `ror8(b^k2,3)^k1`, sha256-check,\n14\tHCFG at out[0]). FIRST day whose prompt theme WAS asked on its own group: config_* only after unpacking + NEW `overlay_offset`\n15\t(offset of the last magic) / `overlay_size` (file length - offset). The question text spelled the whole stub; 228 ids = 216 + 12,\n16\tno backfill; CORRECT T+2:25, TT 4 s / Mastery (5 sets) 10 s first try; overlay 10808/424 constant across variants.\n17\t**Forward hints in the D19 contract**: `overlay_offset` says \"PK19 for Day 19 or RS20 for Day 20\" (=> D20 = another packed overlay,\n18\tmagic `RS20`, probably a new language + a different stub); the `format` enum (d12-d19) lists `neko_bytecode` (=> a Neko VM `.n`\n19\tmember is scheduled, magic `NEKO`).\n20\tLessons for D20+: (a) read the longest question of each new family first -- since D17 the questions are executable specs (rules,\n21\toffsets, transforms, hashes); (b) grep each new contract for tokens/days that are not today's (D19 leaked D20's magic and a future\n22\tcontainer); (c) the new member's header ids keep being answered by the carried-over solver at T+~20 s, the day's twist is in the\n23\tnew field family; (d) `none` is for ABSENT things, never for hidden ones (D19 race placeholders rejected); (e) unguessable labels\n24\tare fixed by the organizers' contract revision -- re-pull instead of guessing.\n25\tAsked field names: config_*, format (enum), machine, architecture, elf_class, elf_type, endianness, entry_point, symbols,\n26\tsection_names, disassembly, marker, recover_code, has_symtab, has_cpp_*, has_go_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol,\n27\thas_coroutine_runtime, mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, methods, access_flags, method_count, has_hcfg_section, hcfg_offset,\n28\thcfg_version, hcfg_storage (enum), xor_key_hex, metadata_version, compression_methods, overlay_offset, overlay_size.\n29\tRemaining risks: (1) D20 `RS20` with an unspecified or mutated stub (rolling key, RLE/LZ, RC4, multi-layer) -- the question text\n30\tshould spell it, the solver must interpret it generically; (2) backfill on d19 asking the overlay header facts (k1, k2,\n31\tpacked_length, unpacked_sha256, overlay_version) or `hcfg_storage` for a packed blob; (3) Neko bytecode container labels\n32\t(architecture/machine for a VM: unknown); (4) per-language fact backfills (D8-D19 groups); (5) the D18 theme family as fields.\n33\t\n34\tTool legend: **[I]** installed (`source bin/env.sh`; checked with `which`/`ls`), **[M]** missing.\n35\tInstalled: readelf/objdump/nm/c++filt/strings/objcopy (binutils x86-64 + aarch64-linux-gnu-objdump), llvm-18 (llvm-objdump-18,\n36\tllvm-readobj-18, llvm-otool, llvm-lipo, llvm-nm, llvm-dwarfdump, llvm-cxxfilt-18 under /usr/lib/llvm-18/bin), file, binwalk, upx 4.2.4,\n37\trizin 0.9.1 (`bin/rizin`, `rz-bin`, `rz-asm`, `rz-find`, `rz-diff`) + radare2/rabin2, Ghidra (`bin/analyzeHeadless`, processors incl.\n38\tAARCH64/ARM/MIPS/PowerPC/RISCV/Sparc/x86/JVM/Dalvik), GoReSym, rustfilt, swift-demangle, nim-demangle, ilspycmd, dotnet, java/javap,\n39\tjadx, dex2jar, apktool, pyinstxtractor, pycdc/pycdas, autoit-ripper, hbc-decompiler, gdb + gdb-multiarch, ltrace/strace, yara, wabt (wasm-objdump/wasm2wat/wat2wasm/wasm-decompile), floss (.venv), luac,\n40\t7z, xxd; venv python: capstone, unicorn, angr, lief, pyelftools, pefile, dnfile, pycryptodome, pyzipper, xdis/uncompyle6/decompyle3,\n41\tlz4, yara. Cross compilers: aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc-15, clang-18 (no lld/wasm-ld: other targets compile to `.o` only).\n42\tMissing: qemu-user(-static), wasm-ld/lld, wasmtime, capa, Detect-It-Easy (diec), de4dot, monodis, erlang (beam_disasm),\n43\tunluac/luajit-decompiler (luac present), blutter, srecord (srec_cat), binutils-multiarch, checksec, python zstandard/brotli, rzpipe/r2pipe.\n44\t\n45\t## Concept table\n46\t\n47\t| # | concept | status | recognition cues | standard tool + exact command | D20+ likelihood |\n48\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n49\t| 1 | C ELF (gcc, glibc) | seen D1, D15 (+ every day's d01; D17 re-asked marker/recover_code) | `GCC: (...)` in `.comment`, `.interp` ld-linux, `__libc_start_main` | [I] `readelf -hSW f; readelf -sW f; objdump -d -M intel f` | high (carry-over every day; mastery d01 re-rolls stripped/renamed) |\n50\t| 2 | C++ Itanium ELF / MinGW PE32+ | seen D2 | `_Z` symbols, `_ZTV`/`_ZTI`/`_ZTS`, `libstdc++`; PE `.text$_Z...` COMDAT, `.CRT`, `.tls` | [I] `nm -C f`; `objdump -t f.exe`; `c++filt` | high (carry-over; ELF/PE re-rolls per member) |\n51\t| 3 | .NET C# PE (pe_cli) | seen D3 | `BSJB` metadata root `v4.0.30319`, `mscoree.dll`/`_CorExeMain`, `.runtimeconfig.json` | [I] `ilspycmd f.dll`; python `dnfile` | high (carry-over) |\n52\t| 4 | Go (static, stripped; PE in Mastery) | seen D4 | `\\xff Go buildinf:`, `.gopclntab`, `runtime.`, `go1.NN` | [I] `GoReSym -t -d -p f`; `go version -m f`; `lib.binary.go_buildinfo` | high (carry-over) |\n53\t| 5 | Rust ELF (debug_info) | seen D5 | `_ZN...17h<16hex>E` / `_R` v0 symbols, `rustc version`, `/rustc/<sha>/library` panic paths | [I] `rustfilt < syms`; `readelf -p .comment f` | high (carry-over) |\n54\t| 6 | Rust stripped / release | gap | no `.symtab`, panic strings + `/rustc/<40hex>/` paths remain, `core::fmt` strings | [I] `strings -a f \\| grep -m3 /rustc/`; Ghidra headless; [M] no cargo-rustc symbol-recovery tool | med (natural \"stripped\" sequel for any language) |\n55\t| 7 | Java / Kotlin jar | seen D6, D7 (D17 re-asked methods/access_flags/method_count/has_coroutine_runtime) | `PK` + `META-INF/MANIFEST.MF`, `CAFEBABE` classes, `kotlin/` packages | [I] `unzip -l f.jar; javap -v -p -c Main.class`; `jadx -d out f.jar`; `lib.binary.jar_app_classes` | high (carry-over) |\n56\t| 8 | Swift ELF (static stdlib, 67 MB) | seen D8 | `swift5_*` sections, `$s` symbols, `libswiftCore` | [I] `bin/swift-demangle`; regex `SENGR` in `.rodata` | high (carry-over) |\n57\t| 9 | Nim / D / Crystal ELF | seen D9, D11, D13 | Nim `NimMain`,`fatal.nim`; D `_D4core`,`DMDH`; Crystal `Crystal:H`,`GC_malloc` | [I] `bin/nim-demangle`; `grep -abo 'SENGR[A-Za-z0-9+/=]*' f` | high (carry-over) |\n58\t| 10 | Zig ELF + PE | seen D10 | `.comment` \"zig-bootstrap\"/LLD 19, stripped, `.hcfg` section | [I] `readelf -p .comment f; readelf -x .hcfg f` | high (carry-over) |\n59\t| 11 | Free Pascal ELF | seen D12 | `FPC 3.2.2`, `.fpcdata`, `FPC_` symbols, static stripped | [I] `strings -a f \\| grep FPC`; `grep -abo HCFG