d, never on field name.\n  no .symtab => stripped (answer [] / none / false); no INTERP => static; ET_DYN+INTERP => PIE; ET_REL => object file\n  UPX0/UPX1 sections or \"UPX!\" or entropy>7.2 => PACKED: upx -t F; cp F /tmp/x; upx -d /tmp/x (fix zeroed UPX! first)\nSTEP 3  strings -a -n6 F | grep -m8 -E 'GCC:|clang|rustc|go1\\.|GHC |OCaml|caml_|FPC |Crystal|zig|GNAT Version|gfortran|DMD|Nim|\n        swift|_kDart|kfun:|__svm|MEI|nuitka|AU3!|Borland|MSVBVM|libcob|UPX|HCFG|SENGR'   -> toolchain + blob form\n  toolchain -> tool: Go GoReSym -t -d -p | Rust rustfilt | .NET ilspycmd | jar javap -v -p / jadx | Swift swift-demangle\n  Nim nim-demangle | PyInstaller pyinstxtractor+pycdc | AutoIt autoit-ripper | anything else: rizin -q -c 'aaa;afl' /\n  analyzeHeadless (lib.binary.ghidra_decompile) | foreign arch: rizin -a <arch> / llvm-objdump-18 / Ghidra (no exec, qemu absent)\nHCFG (every new member since D2)\n  python: from lib.binary import hcfg_find, hcfg_scan; hcfg_find(open(F,'rb').read())  -> config, offset, encoding, key, crc_ok\n  raw magic 'HCFG' | b64 'SENGR' | hex '48434647' | rot13 'FRATE' | b64-zlib 'eJ' | b64-gzip 'H4sI' -> covered by hcfg_scan\n  accept only crc32(plain)==header crc AND JSON parses; keep scanning past decoys (D9 had two raw-magic decoys)\n  NOT FOUND => blob is hidden: (0) OVERLAY past the image end (D19): image_end = e_shoff+e_shnum*e_shentsize (or max\n  section/segment end; PE: pefile overlay start); bytes there start with a day magic (PK19 D19, RS20 announced for D20) ->\n  o = data.rfind(magic) (\"final\"); parse the header fields the QUESTION lists; apply its byte transform (D19:\n  ror8(b^k2,3)^k1); verify its sha256; HCFG at out[0]. overlay_offset = o, overlay_size = len(data)-o; (1) packed? unpack; (2) AES S-box 637c777b / TEA 9e3779b9 / 'expand 32-byte k' => find key+IV\n  near the call, decrypt with pycryptodome; (3) runs of mov [rbp-x], imm => stack-built: collect imms with capstone or\n  emulate the builder with unicorn; (4) PE .rsrc / .NET resource / jar non-class entry / overlay past last section;\n  (5) .init_array / TLS callback decoder => emulate it. Offsets: raw=the H, base64=the S (GM-confirmed); else first stored byte.\nFIELDS: format = container only (elf/pe/macho?/jar; .NET pe_cli) | machine/architecture = container machine word |\n  qualifier ids dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field> -> member whose file name has <tag> (D15 stripped/symbolized, D16 compact/direct;\n  match the LONGEST member-name token, a tag may contain `_`) ; sha256_K = zip archive order | config_* verbatim from HCFG JSON |\n  has_<x>_section = literal section name | hex fields lowercase 0x | never chase the prompt's theme: answer only asked ids.\n  D17 Ada, D18 Fortran, D19 GnuCOBOL (libcob.so.1, cob_* imports, *.cob): plain ELF -> header ids from the carried-over\n  solver (post first, T+~20 s). The day's twist sits in the NEW field family: read its longest question first -- since D17\n  the question text is an executable spec (rules, offsets, transforms, hashes). `none` only for ABSENT things.\nTHEME FACTS (unasked so far, backfill candidates): every member D2+ embeds a huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1 JSON template\n  (branch, event_count, family \"<lang>_<theme>_trace\", effects, network) gated on env HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL (analysis/sandbox/\n  workstation). D18 flow: getenv -> _gfortran_select_string(case table jumptable.N.M) -> mov eax,<event_fn>; call rax.\n  Call graph: capstone direct call rel32 + resolve `call reg` from the preceding mov/lea imm; API intent from UND imports.\nBACKFILL ids on OLD groups (D8, D17): an unknown field on dNN = that day's own facts. Seen: marker (.huntress string),\n  recover_code (decimal imm), mangled_score_symbol/typeinfo_symbol (bare _ZNK.../_ZTI...; PE .text$/.rdata$), has_go_runtime,\n  has_rust_mangled_symbol, has_coroutine_runtime (enum true/false), methods (Main-Class method_info names incl <init>, JSON),\n  access_flags (decimal, 49), method_count (incl <init>/<clinit>). Derive from bytes, POST all derivable ones together.\nhcfg_storage (enum): base64 carrier -> base64 | literal HCFG in section `.hcfg` -> raw_hcfg_section | in WASM data seg ->\n  wasm_data_segment | in another native data section (.data/.rodata) -> raw_const_array | else raw. Stripped d01 => recover_code none.\nUNGUESSABLE label: ~10 single-id probes max, HELP.md, then re-pull the contract (organizers revise it: enum + rule text).\nFORWARD HINTS: grep each new contract for tokens/days that are not today's (D19: `RS20 for Day 20`, enum `neko_bytecode`).\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"contract-revision-watch\", \"concept\": \"Organizers revise the live contract mid-day (D17: exact_text -> enum + rule text)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"When an exact_text label resists ~10 probes: write HELP, then re-pull the contract (`hctf status <id>`) every ~20-30 min and diff question text/answer_format per id; D17 the revision converted ~3.5 h and ~10.9k rejected probes into CORRECT within a minute. Never run mass automated label grouptests on a closed-vocabulary GM field.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"contract-forward-hints\", \"concept\": \"The live contract leaks upcoming days: tokens and day numbers that do not belong to today\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19: the format enum on d12-d19 lists `neko_bytecode` (never seen) and overlay_offset says 'PK19 for Day 19 or RS20 for Day 20'. Each day, grep the contract for magic-like tokens (`[A-Z]{2}\\\\d{2}`), enum values never confirmed, and 'Day NN' > today; record them in solver/NOTES.md and the coverage atlas so the prebuild targets them. The d19 solver already maps a `<2 caps><NN>` magic to the group whose day is NN.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"question-spec-overlay-unpacker\", \"concept\": \"Generic overlay unpacker driven by the QUESTION TEXT: magic, header field offsets/widths, keys, packed length, hash, per-byte transform expression\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19 config questions said: 'Find the final PK19 overlay. Read k1 at +5, k2 at +6, packed length u32le at +8, the 32-byte unpacked SHA-256 at +12, and packed bytes at +44. For each packed byte compute ror8(byte XOR k2,3) XOR k1; verify the unpacked SHA-256 and use the HCFG record at unpacked offset 0.' D20 announces `RS20` with a likely different layout. Build lib.binary.overlay_spec(question) -> {magic, fields{name:(off, fmt u8/u16le/u32le/u32be/bytes[n])}, data_off, hash(sha256/crc32/md5, field), transform AST} and overlay_unpack(data, spec) -> (offset, size, header, out, hash_ok). Transform grammar: XOR/ADD/SUB (mod 256), ror8/rol8(x,n), NOT, nibble swap, index terms (i, i mod n, key[i % len]), previous-byte chaining (prev plain/cipher), reversed order, keystream words (RC4(key), LCG(seed,a,c)), followed by optional zlib/lzma/RLE decompress. Reject (return None) when the hash fails; never guess. Fixtures: the cached D19 member (single + the Mastery/TT deliveries if cached) and synthetic RS20-style overlays for each grammar item with their question sentences; the D19 solver's overlay_unpack/overlay_magic in challenges/day19/binary-jack-in-the-box/solver/solve.py is the reference.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"rs20-overlay-candidates\", \"concept\": \"Day 20 `RS20` overlay (named in the D19 contract): fixtures and decoders for the likely 'RS' stubs\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19 overlay_offset question: 'Locate the final overlay magic named by this unit (PK19 for Day 19 or RS20 for Day 20)'. RS guesses, each as a synthetic ELF + appended `RS20` overlay with a sha256 of the unpacked HCFG and a question-style sentence: (a) RLE stream (count,byte pairs / PackBits), (b) rolling xor stream (key = key*mul+add per byte, or key ^= prev), (c) RC4 keystream with key bytes in the header, (d) reversed + rotated segments ('reverse-shuffle'), (e) rotate-by-index ror8(b, i%8), (f) zlib/LZSS after a byte map. Ensure overlay_offset = last `RS20` start and overlay_size = len - offset still hold, and the known-plaintext fallback (out starts with `HCFG`, ver 1, len = packed_len - 12) recovers unstated keys. Feed every fixture through question-spec-overlay-unpacker.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"neko-bytecode-member\", \"concept\": \"Neko VM bytecode member (`.n`, magic NEKO): container parse, globals/strings, HCFG location, labels for format/architecture/machine\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The GM's own format enum (d12-d19 since D19) lists `neko_bytecode` = a Neko member is scheduled. `apt install neko haxe` (candidates neko 2.4.1, haxe 4.3.7) then build fixtures: a Haxe `-neko out.n` program and a raw `nekoc` program holding the HCFG as a string literal (raw bytes and base64 'SENGR...') -- plus `nekotools boot` (Neko standalone ELF = neko VM + appended bytecode, another overlay!). Parser: 'NEKO' u32 nglobals, u32 nfields, u32 codesize; globals (type byte: 1 var, 2 function, 3 string u16/u32 len, 4 float, 5 debug, 6 version), fields (NUL-terminated names), code. Facts: format `neko_bytecode`, globals_count, fields list, string globals, hcfg offset (start of the string payload = the `H`/`S`), has_neko_runtime; architecture/machine for a VM are UNKNOWN -- record candidates (`neko`, `nekovm`, `none`) and read the question text first. Ensure lib.binary magic dispatch and the solver's format() return `neko_bytecode` for raw .n and recognise a nekotools-booted ELF (format elf + overlay).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"overlay-header-facts\", \"concept\": \"Overlay/packer header facts as fields for the d19 group (and RS20): has_overlay, overlay_magic, overlay_version, k1_hex/k2_hex, packed_length, unpacked_size, unpacked_sha256, image_end\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19 asked only overlay_offset/overlay_size + config after unpacking; the D17 pattern means the header fields get asked within days (or on the d19 group in a backfill). From the PK19 header: magic `PK19`, version byte 4 (1), k1 byte 5 / k2 byte 6 as `0x%02x` (like xor_key_hex), pad byte 7, packed_length u32le +8 (380), unpacked_sha256 = 64 lowercase hex (+12..+44, no prefix, like artifact sha256), unpacked_size = len(out), packed_sha256, image_end (e_shoff + e_shnum*e_shentsize) and overlay == image_end boolean, overlay_entropy. Expose in the solver facts dict with plain names (overlay_version, k1_hex, k2_hex, packed_length, unpacked_length, unpacked_sha256, has_overlay=true/false) and a generic hcfg_storage answer for a packed blob (rule list: no section contains it -> `raw`? record as uncertain; read the enum text). Tests: cached D19 member + synthetic overlays.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"theme-facts-recording\", \"concept\": \"Record each day's prompt-theme facts during the single solve (asked on its own day since D19, or in a later backfill)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D5-D18 themes were never asked on their own day, but D19's WAS (overlay_offset/overlay_size + config only after unpacking) and D17 backfilled D1-D7 single-solve facts on their old groups. After CORRECT, spend <=2 min writing the theme facts (stub/overlay header fields, call graph, branch map, imports, trace family/effects, decoder) into solver/NOTES.md under `THEME FACTS dNN:`; the solver's facts dict should already expose them as candidate field names (d19: overlay_version, k1/k2 hex, packed_length, unpacked_size, unpacked_sha256).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"fortran-gfortran-deep-facts\", \"concept\": \"gfortran facts for the d18 group when its theme is backfilled: source file name, MAIN__, internal procedures (name.N), select_string case table, libgfortran imports, .comment GCC banner\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Fixtures: copy the cached d18 members (single variant-000 + TT/Mastery variants under challenges/day18/binary-flow-state/solver/cases/*/artifacts) into tests/data/binary_fixtures (gfortran compiler is NOT installed; runtime libgfortran.so.5 is). Facts: source_file `variant-000.f90` (STT_FILE), main_program `MAIN__`, procedures [event_failure, event_sandbox, event_decoy, event_success] with and without the `.N` suffix (table order + address order), case table = `_gfortran_select_string` struct array {low_ptr, low_len, high_ptr, high_len, case_no} x N (entry 0 = default, NULL ptrs) -> [(case_string, case_no)] e.g. analysis->1, sandbox->2, workstation->3, env var `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL` (the edi string passed to _gfortran_get_environment_variable_i4), imports list (9 `_gfortran_*`), NEEDED [libgfortran.so.5, libm.so.6, libgcc_s.so.1, libc.so.6], hcfg symbol `encoded_config.4`. Expose all as facts-dict keys with plain names (procedures, case_values, env_var, needed, imports, source_file).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"callgraph-indirect-flow-facts\", \"concept\": \"Generic call graph with indirect-call resolution for ELF/PE: per-function callees, PLT import edges, `mov/lea reg, imm; call reg` targets, call-table/jump-table targets, entry->main chain\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D18 prompt: 'Reconstruct the call graph ... follow the calls' (unasked). Implement lib.binary.call_graph(data) with capstone linear sweep over FUNC symbols (fallback: .eh_frame FDE ranges / rizin `aaa;aflj` when stripped): direct `call rel32` -> callee symbol or PLT import name (resolve via .rela.plt), `call reg` resolved by backward scan for `mov e/rax, imm32` or `lea rax, [rip+x]` in the same block, `call [rip+x]` via GOT/data pointer. Output edges [[caller, callee, kind(direct|plt|indirect)]] in address order, plus indirect_call_count, indirect_targets, functions_reached_from(main). Fixtures: d18 Fortran (4 indirect `call rax` to event_*), d01 C, d15 stripped/symbolized pair, a PE (d02 MinGW). Candidate GM shapes: JSON array of callee names, integer counts, `none` when stripped.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"api-intent-injection-classifier\", \"concept\": \"Classify each imported/called API by intent and give an injection verdict (ELF + PE), mapping to MITRE T1055.x\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D18 prompt: 'read the API intent at each edge, and prove no injection hides in the flow'; trace effects `modeled_process_access_no_injection`. Table (lib/knowledge.py-style dict, not lib edits by workers): env_query (getenv, _gfortran_get_environment_variable_i4, GetEnvironmentVariable), output (printf/puts/write/_gfortran_st_write*), string (strcmp/_gfortran_select_string/string_len_trim), process_access (ptrace ATTACH/PEEK, OpenProcess, /proc/<pid>/mem read), injection (ptrace POKETEXT/POKEDATA/SETREGS, process_vm_writev, VirtualAllocEx+WriteProcessMemory+CreateRemoteThread, NtMapViewOfSection, QueueUserAPC, SetWindowsHookEx, SetThreadContext, LD_PRELOAD/dlopen of a written file, memfd_create+execve), network (socket/connect/WSAStartup/WinHttp*). Facts: api_intents {name: intent}, has_injection (true/false), injection_apis [] , process_access_apis. Fixtures: d18 (no injection), plus small gcc/MinGW-free fixtures that import process_vm_writev / ptrace (PE: build import table with pefile or use existing PE fixtures).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dynamic-trace-template-facts\", \"concept\": \"Parse the `huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1` trace template embedded in every member (D2-D18) and model its env-gated branches\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Every member carries a format template like `{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1\\\",\\\"branch\\\":\\\"<b>\\\",\\\"event_count\\\":<n>,\\\"campaign\\\":\\\"BRNN-00V\\\",\\\"family\\\":\\\"fortran_indirect_flow_trace\\\",\\\"effects\\\":\\\"modeled_process_access_no_injection\\\",\\\"network\\\":\\\"none\\\"}` (jar: constant-pool strings; wasm: data segment; some keys filled at runtime: manifest_entries, archive_score, selector `eventCountForModel:` on ObjC). Families seen: d10 non_mutating_service_plan, d11 synthetic_document_manifest, d12 private_scratch_archive_manifest, d14 non_mutating_trigger_plan, d15 symbol_loss_equivalent_trace, d17 ada_encoded_config_trace, d18 fortran_indirect_flow_trace. Extract per member: schema, family, effects, network, static key list, host-model options (`analysis`/`sandbox`/`workstation`), env var name (`HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL`), and the branch/event chosen per option (static from the case table / compare chain; optional sandboxed run under bwrap with --unshare-net and the env set, ELF x86-64 only, never on the host). Facts keys: trace_schema, trace_family, trace_effects, trace_network, host_model_env, host_models, branch_for_<model>.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"hcfg-storage-classifier\", \"concept\": \"Generic `hcfg_storage` token for EVERY group/container per the D17 GM rule list (base64 / raw_hcfg_section / wasm_data_segment / raw_const_array / raw)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D17 asked it on d08/d09/d11-d14 only; the next backfill likely spreads it (as hcfg_offset spread) to d02 (ELF `.hcfg` or PE `.hcfg` COFF section), d03 (.NET FieldRVA blob inside PE `.text` -> by the rules `raw_const_array` only if the section is a data section, else `raw` -- record both as uncertain), d04 Go/d05 Rust/d17 Ada `.rodata` (raw_const_array), d06/d07 jars (base64 in a deflated constant pool -> `base64`), d10 `.hcfg` (raw_hcfg_section), d15 pair, d16 wasm (wasm_data_segment). Implement `lib.binary.hcfg_storage(data, hit)` = rules applied in order over (hit.encoding, container, section containing hit.offset with its flags: SHF_ALLOC && !SHF_EXECINSTR = data; PE IMAGE_SCN_CNT_INITIALIZED_DATA; Mach-O __DATA/__DATA_CONST/__TEXT,__const). Tests: every cached day02-day17 member on disk (GM-confirmed d08/d09/d11-d14 tokens as expected values) + synthetic `.hcfg`/.data/.rodata/.text/PE/wasm fixtures; return None (not a guess) when the hit lies in no section.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"question-rule-extractor\", \"concept\": \"Read the contract's per-id rule text + `accepted_values` and enforce it pre-submit (organizer revisions turn labels into enums)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D17: the organizers re-issued the contract mid-day; hcfg_storage became kind enum with accepted_values and 'Apply these mutually exclusive rules in order: <token> when <cond>; ...; otherwise <token>'. Build a lane helper that (a) parses `(token, condition)` pairs out of such question text, (b) exposes `accepted_values` per id to the solver, (c) refuses to emit a token outside accepted_values (empty + log instead), (d) diffs two contract snapshots per id (question/answer_format changed) so a stuck worker sees the revision immediately. Tests: D17 single_solve morning vs revised contract.json (both on disk if cached; otherwise synthetic pair).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"offset-section-mapper\", \"concept\": \"Map a file offset to its container location: ELF section + segment (name, flags, VA), PE section (name, RVA, VA), Mach-O segment,section, WASM data segment index + memory offset\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Underpins hcfg_storage and the likely next location ids (`hcfg_section`, `hcfg_va`/`hcfg_vaddr`, `hcfg_rva`, `hcfg_segment`, `hcfg_mem_offset`). `lib.binary.locate_offset(data, off)` -> {container, section, section_flags, segment_index, vaddr, rva, wasm_data_index, wasm_mem_offset}; pure struct parsing (no pyelftools exceptions on sstripped files: fall back to program headers). Expected spellings to try first: section name verbatim (`.rodata`), VA as lowercase `0x` hex like entry_point. Tests on cached day08-day17 members (D17 Ada blob at file 207432 in `.rodata`, D14 at 4000 in `.hcfg`, D12 at 82928 in `.data`) and the wasm fixtures.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"elf-header-segment-facts\", \"concept\": \"Remaining ELF header + program-header facts as fields: e_flags, os_abi, abi_version, e_phnum/e_shnum/e_shstrndx, segments list (p_type order), interpreter, GNU_STACK/RELRO/PIE/static booleans\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"NOT BUILT (1st attempt killed rc -9, nothing written: keep the scope small -- pyelftools only, no Ghidra). Backfills so far asked elf_class, elf_type, endianness, entry_point, section_names, symbols, has_symtab. Next cheap carry-over ids: `segments`/`program_headers` (JSON of p_type names readelf-style `LOAD`/`PT_LOAD`? both recorded), `segment_count`, `section_count` (incl. NULL), `interpreter` (`/lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2`), `os_abi` (`UNIX - System V` vs `ELFOSABI_SYSV` vs 0), `is_pie`/`is_static`/`has_nx`/`relro` (`full`/`partial`/`none`), `e_flags` hex. Implement in the solver facts dict (lib.binary helper) with GM-style spellings mirroring the confirmed ones (ET_EXEC style for enums, lowercase 0x hex, decimal counts). Tests: cached day01-day17 ELF members + readelf parity.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ada-gnat-deep-facts\", \"concept\": \"Ada/GNAT facts for the d17 group when its own theme is backfilled: GNAT version, binder/elaboration symbols, Ada subprogram names, decoder function, exception ids\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D17 prompt ('recover the reversible decoder') was unasked; the D17 backfill pattern means d17 facts get asked within days. From the cached Ada ELF (single_solve/work/extracted d17 member): gnat_version (`GNAT Version: 14.2.0` -> `14.2.0`), has_gnat_runtime (`__gnat_`/`ada__`/`system__`), main/binder symbols (`_ada_<main>`, `adainit`, `adafinal`, `__gnat_main`?), Ada-encoded names `pkg__sub` -> `pkg.sub` (keep mangled when asked for symbols), DWARF producer `GNU Ada 14.2.0` / DW_LANG_Ada95/2005, decoder routine name (function whose code xrefs the blob VA, via decoder-routine-locator) and its xor immediate (== header key?). Return none/false on absence; never raise.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"qemu-user-static\", \"concept\": \"Run/observe foreign