huge static binary, `.data` closures. Facts: has_ghc_runtime, z-decoded module names, ghc_version. Risk: a Text literal may be UTF-16 or chunked -> hcfg_scan utf16 + split modes. ghc not installed (apt ghc is ~1 GB): hand-craft fixtures with z-encoded symbol tables on a C ELF and a split-literal blob.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ocaml-native-member\", \"concept\": \"OCaml native ELF (ocamlopt): caml symbols, string literals with OCaml block headers, HCFG offset convention\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Cues: `caml_startup`, `caml_main`, `camlStdlib__`, `camlDune__exe__Main`, `OCAMLRUNPARAM`. OCaml strings are header-prefixed blocks (word header + padded bytes, last byte = pad count) -> HCFG raw starts at the block payload (offset = the `H`, like D12/D14). Facts: has_ocaml_runtime, module names `camlMain__entry`. ocaml not installed: synthesize a C ELF with OCaml-shaped symbols + a block-wrapped blob.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"kotlin-native-member\", \"concept\": \"Kotlin/Native ELF (konanc): `kfun:` symbols, Konan runtime, HCFG in an object literal\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Kotlin already appeared as a jar (D7); a native build is a plausible 'pair the language with a new container' twist. Cues: `kfun:` / `kclass:` / `ktype:` symbols, `Konan_main`, `Kotlin_` runtime, `kotlin.native.internal`. Strings are UTF-16 in KString objects -> hcfg_scan utf16 path + offset = first stored byte (speculative). Facts: has_kotlin_native_runtime, kfun names. Fixture: C ELF with those symbol names + UTF-16LE base64 blob.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pe-optional-header-facts\", \"concept\": \"PE/COFF facts for the PE members (d02 MinGW, d03 .NET, d10 Zig PE, d04 Go .exe): subsystem, image_base, timestamp, characteristics, dll_characteristics, section names (NUL-trimmed), entry RVA/VA, imports\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"PE members re-roll into Mastery for d02/d04/d10; a backfill on them would ask the ELF-equivalent fields: format pe, machine, entry_point (ImageBase+AddressOfEntryPoint as 0x hex?), section_names (PE names, `/4` long names resolved via COFF string table), subsystem (`console`/`IMAGE_SUBSYSTEM_WINDOWS_CUI`/3), image_base, has_symtab (COFF symbol table present), timestamp (decimal). pefile installed. Tests: cached MinGW/Zig/Go/.NET PE members from day02-day16 artifacts + record both spelling families.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jumptable-switch-recovery\", \"concept\": \"Recover switch/SELECT CASE dispatch: gcc relative int32 tables (`movsxd rax,[rdx+rax*4]; add rax,rdx; jmp rax`), absolute 8-byte tables, MSVC/MinGW tables, gfortran select_string case arrays, Go/Rust match tables\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 dispatched on `_gfortran_select_string` + cmp chain; a stripped or -O2 sequel uses a real jump table. Implement lib.binary.switch_tables(data): find `jmp reg` preceded by a bounded index (cmp/ja) and a table base (lea rip+x), read N entries, map case -> target address -> symbol. Fixtures: clang-18/gcc -O2 C switch with 6+ dense cases (ELF + `-static`), the d18 case table, an AArch64 `br x` table (aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc). Output: [{case, target, symbol}] and case_count.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"anti-analysis-gating-facts\", \"concept\": \"Anti-analysis / sandbox gating facts: environment and host-model checks, decoy branches, debugger/VM detection (TracerPid, ptrace TRACEME, CPUID hypervisor bit, DMI/VM vendor strings, rdtsc timing)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 had event_sandbox/event_decoy branches selected by HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL -- an 'evasion' theme is a natural next day. Facts: anti_debug (bool + technique list: ptrace_traceme, tracerpid, isdebuggerpresent, ntqueryinformationprocess, timing), anti_vm (cpuid_hypervisor, vm_strings list), env_gates [env var names compared], decoy_functions (symbols named *decoy*, or branches that skip the HCFG). MITRE T1497 / T1622. Fixtures: small gcc C ELFs with each check (static analysis only; never execute).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"flattened-dispatcher-recovery\", \"concept\": \"Control-flow flattening (OLLVM-style state-variable dispatcher) and opaque predicates: recover the original block order / state transitions\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Title pun 'Flow State' -> state machine; OLLVM is not installed, so hand-write fixtures: C with `switch(state)` inside `while(1)` where each case sets the next state (constants xor'd), plus opaque predicates `x*(x+1)%2==0`. Extractor: identify the dispatcher (block with most predecessors + cmp/jmp on one stack var), emulate each case with unicorn to read the next-state constant, output the state sequence [s0, s1, ...], the executed block order, and the final return value (ties into emulate-return-value). Fixtures in ELF x86-64 and one MinGW-free PE via existing PE fixture style.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"gcc-frontend-modula2-member\", \"concept\": \"Next GCC front-end languages as a new-day member: Modula-2 (gm2), COBOL (gcobol, GCC 15), Algol 68 (ga68), gccgo\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"NOT BUILT (1st attempt failed). D17 Ada, D18 Fortran, D19 GnuCOBOL: the organizers walk a 'legacy/GCC-family language' list, each lan","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/1f691966-10aa-49ba-9a5a-93650aac521b/tool-results/beom24enw.txt","persistedOutputSize":51077},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01H8hNdKSTPTAphmZDGHrGff","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
