erlay at e_shoff+e_shnum*64: `RS20|ver@4|u32le res_len@8|u16le scratch_len@12|sha256(scratch)@16|HCFG resource@48 (RAW)|\nscratch` (\"private-scratch:<campaign>:inert-only\"). 240 ids = 228 + 12; NEW `hcfg_resource_size` (= u32le @8, 380). The prebuilt\nRS20/question-spec unpacker + raw HCFG scan banked 239 ids at T+27 s; one field branch -> CORRECT T+49 s, 0 wrong; TT 4.8 s /\nMastery 9.3 s first try; overlay constant across variants. D19-D20 = a \"hidden storage\" arc (packed overlay -> resource overlay;\nprompt: \"resources, overlays, bytes past the end of the sections ... map every boundary\").\n**Forward hints still open**: `neko_bytecode` in the format enum (unseen through D20); d07 `method_count` text: \"for Day 26 use the\nprimary classfile named by that unit\" (=> a JVM classfile member on D26 whose primary class is named by the question, not the\nmanifest). No new magic token in the D20 contract (no `XX21`): D21's twist is unannounced.\nLessons for D21+: (a) read the longest question of each new family first -- it is the layout spec; (b) every `*_size`/`*_offset`/\n`*_sha256` id maps to ONE named header field: parse the spec into a struct and expose every field; (c) grep each contract for\ntokens/days that are not today's; (d) header ids of the new member are answered by the carried-over solver; the twist is the new\nfield family; (e) `none` only for ABSENT things; (f) unguessable labels get fixed by contract revision -- re-pull.\n'''+t[b:]\nrep(\"hcfg_version, hcfg_storage (enum), xor_key_hex, metadata_version, compression_methods, overlay_offset, overlay_size.\",\n    \"hcfg_version, hcfg_storage (enum), xor_key_hex, metadata_version, compression_methods, overlay_offset, overlay_size,\\nhcfg_resource_size.\")\na=t.index(\"Remaining risks: (1) D20\"); b=t.index(\"Tool legend:\")\nt=t[:a]+'''Remaining risks: (1) D21 continues the storage arc with an unannounced container spot (section slack/caves, ELF notes,\ncompressed sections, multi-entry resource tables, appended archives, PE .rsrc/certificate) -- the question will spell the layout;\n(2) a backfill asking RS20/PK19 header facts (scratch_size, scratch_sha256, overlay_version, k1/k2, packed_length) or\n`hcfg_storage` for overlay-stored blobs; (3) Neko bytecode labels (architecture/machine for a VM); (4) D26 JVM classfile member;\n(5) per-language fact backfills (D8-D20 groups).\n\n'''+t[b:]\n# table rows\nrep(\"| 13 | Haskell (GHC) | gap | `hs_main`, `ghczmprim_`/`base_GHCziBase` z-encoded symbols, `GHC <ver>` rts strings, huge static ELF | [I] `strings -a f \\\\| grep -m2 'GHC '`; `nm f \\\\| grep -c _info$`; [M] no hsdecomp | med (classic \\\"weird runtime\\\" language left on the list) |\",\n    \"| 13 | Haskell (GHC) | **seen D20** (GHC 9.12.2, 1.2 MB DYNAMIC (libgmp/libm/libc), gold, not stripped, config in the RS20 overlay, not the image) | `Main_main*_closure`/`_info`, z-encoded `ghczminternal_GHCziInternalzi*`, `UnitLinkOpts {hsLibs = [\\\"-lHSbase-4.21...` string, `.debug-ghc-link-info` section, `.note.gnu.gold-version` | [I] `strings -a f \\\\| grep -m2 -E 'GHC [0-9]\\\\|hsLibs'`; `nm f \\\\| grep -c _info$`; [M] ghc, hsdecomp | high (carry-over; its theme facts = backfill candidates) |\")\nrep(\"| 56 | Resources: PE RT_RCDATA, .NET manifest resource, jar non-class file, Mach-O section | prebuilt (resource-overlay-hcfg) |\",\n    \"| 56 | Resources: PE RT_RCDATA, .NET manifest resource, jar non-class file, Mach-O section | prebuilt (resource-overlay-hcfg); D20's \\\"resource\\\" was an ELF overlay record, not a real container resource |\")\nrep(\"| 57 | Overlay (bytes after last section / appended) | **seen D19** (PK19 at e_shoff+e_shnum*64 = 10808, 424 B; `overlay_offset`/`overlay_size` asked) |\",\n    \"| 57 | Overlay (bytes after last section / appended) | **seen D19, D20** (PK19 10808/424 B; RS20 1200888/463 B; both at e_shoff+e_shnum*e_shentsize; `overlay_offset`/`overlay_size` asked) |\")\nrep(\"| high (D20 `RS20` named; offset = the magic, size = len - offset) |\",\"| high (2 days running; offset = the magic, size = len - offset) |\")\ni=t.index(\"| 83 | `RS20` overlay\"); j=t.index(\"\\n\",i)\nt=t[:i]+\"| 83 | `RS20` resource overlay | **seen D20** (`RS20|ver@4|u32le res_len@8|u16le scratch_len@12|sha256(scratch)@16|HCFG@48 RAW|scratch`, exact end bounds `48+res+scratch == len-o`) | magic past the image end, plain `HCFG` 48 bytes after it, trailing printable `private-scratch:...` | [I] python: `o=data.rfind(b'RS20')`; `struct.unpack_from('<IH',data,o+8)`; sha256 check; HCFG at o+48; `hcfg_resource_size` = u32 @8 | high (carry-over; mutations may move/resize fields -> parse the question) |\"+t[j:]\nrows='''\n| 87 | Multi-entry resource table / directory overlay (N entries: name/type, offset, size, hash) | gap (D20 had ONE resource + scratch) | count field + fixed-size entry records after the magic; several printable names; offsets relative to the overlay or file | [I] python struct per the question; select the entry by name; verify each hash | high (natural \"map every boundary\" escalation) |\n| 88 | Slack / cave storage: bytes between sections, after a section inside its segment, between the program headers and the first section, before the section-header table | gap (\"bytes past the end of the sections\" in the D20 prompt) | file ranges not covered by any section header (or segment); non-zero padding; HCFG raw scan hit whose offset maps to NO section | [I] pyelftools: sort (sh_offset, sh_size) of non-NOBITS sections, list the gaps; `lib.binary` offset-section mapper | high |\n| 89 | ELF notes as storage (custom `.note.<vendor>` / PT_NOTE: namesz, descsz, type, 4/8-aligned) | gap (`.note.gnu.build-id`, `.note.ABI-tag`, gold-version seen) | `readelf -nW` shows an unknown owner/type; HCFG inside a note desc | [I] `readelf -nW f`; pyelftools `iter_notes()` | med-high |\n| 90 | Compressed sections (SHF_COMPRESSED Elf64_Chdr zlib/zstd; legacy `.zdebug_*` `ZLIB`+u64be size) | gap | `C` flag in `readelf -S`; section starts `01 00 00 00` (ch_type zlib) | [I] `readelf -zx .sec f`; `objcopy --decompress-debug-sections`; python zlib; [M] python zstandard | med |\n| 91 | Appended archive / SFX (zip, tar, 7z, squashfs AppImage, cpio) after an executable; zipapp/escript/SWI-Prolog saved states | gap | `PK\\\\x05\\\\x06` EOCD near EOF with offsets relative to the archive start; `hsqs` squashfs; `7z\\\\xbc\\\\xaf` | [I] python zipfile (handles prepended data), `7z l f`, `binwalk f`, `unsquashfs` | med-high |\n| 92 | JS runtime single executables: Node SEA (`NODE_SEA_BLOB` note/resource + fuse sentinel), Deno (`d3n0l4nd` trailer), Bun (`---- Bun! ----` trailer), pkg/nexe | gap | huge ELF (80-120 MB) + trailer with offsets; JS source text holding a base64 HCFG | [I] python trailer parse; `strings -a f \\\\| grep -m3 -E 'NODE_SEA\\\\|d3n0l4nd\\\\|Bun!'` | med (resource-embedding runtimes fit the arc) |\n| 93 | JVM-language classfile member on D26 (Scala/Clojure/Groovy/standalone `.class`), \"primary classfile named by that unit\" | gap (leaked in the D19/D20 d07 method_count text) | `CAFEBABE` standalone or jar without a usable Main-Class; `ScalaSignature`, Clojure `__init`, Groovy `$getStaticMetaClass` | [I] `javap -v -p`; `lib.binary.jar_app_classes`; jadx | med (6 days out) |'''\ni=t.index(\"\\n## Recognition cues\"); \nk=t.rindex(\"\\n\",0,i-1)\nt=t[:i].rstrip(\"\\n\")+rows+\"\\n\"+t[i:]\n# recognition cues edits\nrep(\"\"\"  NOT FOUND => blob is hidden: (0) OVERLAY past the image end (D19): image_end = e_shoff+e_shnum*e_shentsize (or max\n  section/segment end; PE: pefile overlay start); bytes there start with a day magic (PK19 D19, RS20 announced for D20) ->\n  o = data.rfind(magic) (\"final\"); parse the header fields the QUESTION lists; apply its byte transform (D19:\n  ror8(b^k2,3)^k1); verify its sha256; HCFG at out[0]. overlay_offset = o, overlay_size = len(data)-o;\"\"\",\n\"\"\"  ALWAYS check the tail: image_end = e_shoff+e_shnum*e_shentsize (or max section/segment end; PE: pefile overlay start);\n  len > image_end => OVERLAY with a day magic (PK19 D19 packed; RS20 D20 = raw HCFG @+48 + scratch, res_len u32@8,\n  scratch_len u16@12, sha256(scratch)@16). o = data.rfind(magic) (\"final\"); parse EVERY header field the QUESTION lists into\n  a dict (size ids = that field, e.g. hcfg_resource_size = u32@8); verify its bounds/sha256; run its transform (D19\n  ror8(b^k2,3)^k1); HCFG at the stated offset. overlay_offset = o, overlay_size = len(data)-o.\n  NOT FOUND => hidden elsewhere:\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  D17 Ada, D18 Fortran, D19 GnuCOBOL (libcob.so.1, cob_* imports, *.cob): plain ELF -> header ids from the carried-over\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"  D17 Ada, D18 Fortran, D19 GnuCOBOL, D20 Haskell (GHC; hsLibs/z-encoded closures): plain ELF -> header ids from the carried-over\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"FORWARD HINTS: grep each new contract for tokens/days that are not today's (D19: `RS20 for Day 20`, enum `neko_bytecode`).\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"FORWARD HINTS: grep each new contract for tokens/days that are not today's (D19 `RS20 for Day 20` came true; open: enum\n  `neko_bytecode`, \"for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit\" on d07 method_count).\"\"\")\n# gaps\nm=re.search(r'## Readiness gaps\\n```json\\n(.*?)\\n```',t,re.S)\ng=json.loads(m.group(1))\ng=[x for x in g if x['id'] not in ('rs20-overlay-candidates','haskell-ghc-member')]\nfor x in g:\n    if x['id']=='contract-forward-hints':\n        x['detail']=(\"D19 leaked D20's overlay magic ('PK19 for Day 19 or RS20 for Day 20') and it came true. Still open after D20: the format enum lists `neko_bytecode` (unseen), and d07_analysis_method_count says 'for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit'. \"\n                     \"Each day, grep the contract for magic-like tokens (`[A-Z]{2}\\\\d{2}`), enum values never confirmed, and 'Day NN' > today; record them in solver/NOTES.md and the coverage atlas so the prebuild targets them. The solver maps a `<2 caps><NN>` magic to the group whose day is NN.\")\n    if x['id']=='theme-facts-recording':\n        x['detail']=x['detail'].replace(\"D5-D18 themes were never asked on their own day, but D19's WAS (overlay_offset/overlay_size + config only after unpacking)\",\n            \"D5-D18 themes were never asked on their own day, but D19's (overlay_offset/overlay_size, config after unpacking) and D20's (overlay_offset, hcfg_resource_size) WERE\")\n        x['detail']+=\" d20: rs20 version, hcfg_resource_size, scratch_size (35), scratch_sha256, scratch text, image_end, GHC version 9.12.2.\"\n    if x['id']=='new-language-fingerprints':\n        x['concept']=\"OCaml, V, Odin, Modula-2, Kotlin/Native, Dart AOT, Nuitka, Erlang, Julia (Ada D17, Fortran D18, COBOL D19, Haskell D20 seen)\"\n        x['detail']=x['detail'].replace(\"Ada landed D17 as a plain ELF with RAW HCFG -- the law held.\",\"Ada/Fortran/COBOL/Haskell all landed as plain x86-64 ELFs (format elf) -- the law held; D19-D20 moved the HCFG into an overlay instead.\")\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"question-layout-parser-mutations\",\"concept\":\"Turn the question's layout prose into a struct and expose EVERY named field (any `<name>_size/_length/_offset/_sha256/_version/_count` id), robust to TT/Mastery mutations of the header\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D20 needed a hand-written branch for the one unknown id (`hcfg_resource_size` = 'HCFG resource length u32le at +8'). Build lib.binary.layout_from_question(text) -> [(name, offset, type)] parsing phrases seen D19-D20: 'Read k1 at +5', 'X length u32le at +8', 'scratch length u16le at +12', 'bytes +16..+47 are the scratch SHA-256', 'the HCFG resource starts at +48, and scratch follows it', 'Verify exact end bounds'; also u8/u16be/u32be/u64le, 'relative to the overlay/file', 'immediately after'. Return a facts dict (fields + derived starts/ends + bound/hash checks) the solver can answer any matching id from by fuzzy name (resource_size == resource length). Fixtures: synthetic overlays with permuted fields, BE ints, renamed magic, extra padding, each with its question text; test that every id resolves.\"},\n {\"id\":\"resource-table-overlay\",\"concept\":\"Multi-entry resource directory overlays: magic + count + N fixed-size entries (name/type id, offset, size, sha256/crc) + data, select the HCFG entry by name/type\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Natural escalation of D20's single-resource RS20 ('map every boundary'). Synthetic fixtures: ELF + appended table with 2-5 entries (HCFG, decoy HCFG with bad crc, scratch, icon), offsets relative to the overlay vs the file, names as fixed 8-byte/NUL-padded or length-prefixed strings. Fields to expose: resource_count, resource_names (JSON, table order), per-entry offset/size/sha256, selected entry index, boundaries [[start,end],...]. Reuse question-layout-parser output for the header.\"},\n {\"id\":\"section-slack-cave-storage\",\"concept\":\"Bytes past the end of the sections but INSIDE the image: inter-section padding, section tail slack inside its PT_LOAD segment, gap between program headers and the first section, gap before the section-header table\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D20 prompt: 'bytes past the end of the sections ... map every boundary'. Build lib.binary.elf_file_map(data) -> ordered list of covered ranges (ELF header, PHDRs, each non-NOBITS section, SHT, overlay) and UNCOVERED gaps with (start, end, size, entropy, nonzero bytes, containing segment). Fixtures: gcc ELF with HCFG patched into the alignment gap before .text / after .rodata / before e_shoff, and one with the gap inside a PT_LOAD (code cave). Fields: cave_offset/size, gap list JSON, hcfg_storage for a gap (probably `raw` per the D17 rule list). Same for PE (between section raw ends and next PointerToRawData).\"},\n {\"id\":\"appended-archive-sfx\",\"concept\":\"Archive appended to an executable (zip/escript/SWI-Prolog saved state/zipapp, tar, 7z, squashfs AppImage, cpio): find it, fix relative offsets, read the HCFG member\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Cues: `PK\\\\x05\\\\x06` EOCD near EOF whose cd_offset is relative to the archive start (python zipfile tolerates prepended data; record archive_start = len - (eocd_off - cd_offset ... )), `hsqs` squashfs (AppImage runtime ELF + squashfs at the ELF image end), `7z\\\\xbc\\\\xaf\\\\x27\\\\x1c`, `ustar` at +257. Fixtures: ELF + zip(HCFG.json), ELF + tar, ELF + squashfs (mksquashfs if installed, else synthetic header only). Expose archive_offset, archive_format, member names (central-directory order), member sha256. AES zip inside? use the GM password `infected` only if the question says so.\"},\n {\"id\":\"elf-notes-custom-storage\",\"concept\":\"HCFG stored in a custom ELF note (SHT_NOTE `.note.<vendor>` / PT_NOTE): namesz/descsz/type parsing with 4/8 alignment\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Fixture: gcc ELF with `objcopy --add-section .note.huntress=note.bin --set-section-flags .note.huntress=alloc,readonly` (+ a PT_NOTE variant via linker script). Parser: pyelftools iter_notes + raw fallback walking (namesz, descsz, type) with alignment. Expose note owners/types JSON in table order, the desc offset of the HCFG (offset convention: the `H`), has_<owner>_note.\"},\n {\"id\":\"compressed-elf-sections\",\"concept\":\"SHF_COMPRESSED sections (Elf64_Chdr ch_type 1 zlib / 2 zstd) and legacy `.zdebug_*` (`ZLIB` + u64be size) holding the HCFG\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Fixtures: `objcopy --add-section .hcfg=blob --compress-debug-sections` does not touch non-debug sections, so write Chdr + zlib manually (ch_type, ch_size, ch_addralign) and set SHF_COMPRESSED (0x800); also a `.zdebug_hcfg` legacy one. Decoder: python zlib; zstd needs `pip install zstandard` into .venv (missing) or the `zstd` CLI. Expose compressed size, uncompressed size (ch_size), ch_type label.\"},\n {\"id\":\"haskell-ghc-deep-facts\",\"concept\":\"GHC + RS20 facts for the d20 group when its theme/identity is backfilled: GHC version, hsLibs/UnitLinkOpts, Main_main closures, has_ghc_runtime, rts options; RS20 header fields\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Fixtures: copy the cached d20 members (single variant-000 + TT/Mastery variants under challenges/day20/binary-resourceful/*/). Facts: ghc_version from the `9.12.2`-style string near `ProjectVersion`/hsLibs (`-lHSghc-internal-9.1202.0`), base version 4.21.0.0, NEEDED [libm, libgmp, libc], `.debug-ghc-link-info` present, gold-version note, symbol count of `_closure`/`_info`, Main module symbols, trace family `haskell_resource_overlay_trace` / effects `private_scratch_hash_only`; RS20: version 1, res_len 380, scratch_len 35, scratch_sha256, scratch text, image_end, overlay_size (463). Expose as facts dict keys matching likely field names.\"},\n {\"id\":\"pe-certificate-overlay\",\"concept\":\"PE overlay coexisting with an Authenticode certificate table (Security directory points into the file tail), PE checksum, overlay start vs cert range\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"If the storage arc moves to PE (d02/d04/d10 already re-roll PE in Mastery): overlay start = max(PointerToRawData+SizeOfRawData); DIRECTORY_ENTRY_SECURITY VirtualAddress is a FILE offset; HCFG may sit after the WIN_CERTIFICATE (dwLength, wRevision 0x0200, wCertificateType 2) or inside its padding. Fixtures: MinGW PE (x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc if present, else pefile-synthesized) + fake WIN_CERTIFICATE + appended blob; fields overlay_offset, certificate_offset/size, checksum valid?\"},\n {\"id\":\"js-runtime-single-executable\",\"concept\":\"Node SEA / Deno compile / Bun --compile / pkg single executables: locate the embedded JS + resources by note/section/trailer\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Node SEA: ELF note/section `NODE_SEA_BLOB` (postject) + fuse string `NODE_SEA_FUSE_fce680ab2cc467b6e072b8b5df1996b2:1`; Deno: trailer `d3n0l4nd` + u64 offsets at EOF; Bun: `\\\\n---- Bun! ----\\\\n` trailer with module graph; pkg: `PAYLOAD_POSITION`/`PRELUDE_POSITION` placeholders. Fixtures can be synthetic (small ELF + trailer layout) since real ones are ~100 MB. Expose embedded_source offset/size, entry name; HCFG via hcfg_scan on the JS text.\"},\n {\"id\":\"jvm-language-family-classfile\",\"concept\":\"D26 JVM classfile member (leaked: 'for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit'): Scala/Clojure/Groovy jars or a standalone .class; pick the class the question names\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Extend the d07 method_count path: accept a classfile name from the question text ('primary classfile named by that unit') instead of the manifest Main-Class; handle a bare `CAFEBABE` member (format label? jar enum token does not fit -> watch the enum), Scala (`ScalaSignature`/`ScalaSig` attribute, `$` companion classes), Clojure (`<ns>__init.class`, `clojure/lang/`), Groovy (`$getStaticMetaClass`, `groovy/lang/`). Fixtures via javac/kotlinc if present, else hand-assembled classfiles.\"},\n {\"id\":\"erlang-elixir-beam-member\",\"concept\":\"Erlang/Elixir BEAM member: `FOR1....BEAM` IFF chunks (AtU8/Atom, Code, LitT zlib, StrT, ExpT/ImpT) and escripts (shebang + zip)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Python chunk parser (4-byte id, u32be size, 4-aligned); LitT = u32be uncompressed size + zlib of external-term-format literals -> HCFG likely a binary literal; escript = text header lines + zip (see appended-archive-sfx). format label unknown (not in the enum) -> submit alone. erlang-base apt available for fixtures.\"},\n {\"id\":\"graalvm-julia-native-image\",\"concept\":\"Heavy AOT images that embed resources: GraalVM native-image (`-H:IncludeResources`, `__svm_` heap), Julia sysimage/PackageCompiler apps\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Cues: GraalVM `com.oracle.svm`, `__svm_vm_target`, `.svm_heap` section, resources stored as byte[] in the image heap (raw HCFG scan likely works); Julia `libjulia`, `jl_` symbols, `sys.so` with `jl_system_image_data`. Fixtures synthetic (section names + blob) unless native-image is installable. Expose has_<runtime>, the section holding the HCFG.\"},\n]\nids={x['id'] for x in g}\nfor x in new: assert x['id'] not in ids\ng=new[:4]+g+new[4:]\n# order: priority asc stable\ng.sort(key=lambda x:x['priority'])\nbody=\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False) for x in g)\nt=t[:m.start(1)]+\"[\\n\"+body+\"\\n]\"+t[m.end(1):]\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\nt=open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md').read()\nm=re.search(r'## Readiness gaps\\n```json\\n(.*?)\\n```',t,re.S); g=json.loads(m.group(1))\ns=json.load(open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/.run/prebuild-state.json'))\nopen_=[x['id'] for x in g if x['action']=='prebuild' and not (s.get('binary-reverse-engineering:'+x['id'],{}).get('ok') or s.get('binary-reverse-engineering:'+x['id'],{}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(g), open_, all(set(x)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'} for x in g))\ncue=t[t.index('## Recognition cues'):t.index('## Readiness gaps')]; print('cue lines',cue.count('\\n'))\nEOF"}}}
